<p>  Durables		177.46  177.30   175.40  175.36   173.74</p>
<p> ORDERS-PCT CHANGES:     Apr--(Prev)	Mar--(Prev)     Feb</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   2.9    2.8	 1.3    1.2     -0.5</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   2.7    2.2	 0.2    0.2	2.0</p>
<p>  Electrical Equipment  -5.7   -5.3	-6.1   -6.0	7.8</p>
<p>  Transport Equipment    3.4    4.5	-3.9   -3.9     -7.2</p>
<p> ORDERS-BLNS OF DLRS:    Apr--(Prev)	Mar--(Prev)     Feb</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	 16.48   16.45    16.02   16.01    15.82</p>
<p>  Industrial Machin.   34.10   33.94    33.21   33.22    33.15</p>
<p>  Electrical Equip.    27.12   27.26    28.77   28.78    30.63</p>
<p>  Transport Equip.     38.95   39.36    37.67   37.68    39.21</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected a 0.8 percent rise in total factory orders for April.</p>
<p>The April inventories-to-shipments ratio was 1.37, down from 1.38 in March.  </p>
<p>The 1.2 percent increase in total shipments in April was the largest since a 2.4 percent increase in April 1996, the department said.</p>
<p>The back-to-back monthly decline in order backlogs in March and April was the first since July and August of 1995.</p>
<p>The department reported initial data on April orders for durable goods on May 28.</p>
